{"chapter": "Mathematical Induction", "exam": "ExamSIDE_JEE_Main", "subject": "Mathematics", "totalTopics": 1, "totalQuestions": 3, "topics": [{"index": 1, "topicId": "648b5a73417cc3fb48d6934f", "title": "Mathematical Induction", "totalQuestions": 3, "questions": [{"_id": "648b5a62417cc3fb48d656d1", "type": "singleCorrect", "level": 2, "questionLabels": [], "previousYearPapers": [{"_id": "615d92eade3d91842a5cf7c5", "examId": "615d76b2c52ffa3c944600df", "heldOn": "2005-04-30T09:00:00.000Z", "isVisible": true, "shortName": "2005", "title": "JEE Main 2005"}], "question": {"text": "If $A=\\left[\\begin{array}{ll}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$ and $I=\\left[\\begin{array}{ll}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]$, then which one of the following holds for all $n \\geq 1$, by the principle of mathematical indunction", "image": null}, "options": [{"id": "qoG9c", "text": "\n$A^n=n A-(n-1) I$\n", "image": null, "isCorrect": true}, {"id": "eLMqp", "text": "\n$A^n=2^{n-1} A-(n-1) I$\n", "image": null, "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "zX6GC", "text": "\n$A^n=n A+(n-1) I$\n", "image": null, "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "Yxhxi", "text": "\n$A^n=2^{n-1} A+(n-1) I$", "image": null, "isCorrect": false}], "correctValue": null, "solution": {"text": "By the principle of mathematical induction (A) is true.", "image": null}, "videoSolution": null, "syllabusCategory": "outOfSyllabus", "questionStructure": ["default"], "previousYear": {"_id": "615d92eade3d91842a5cf7c5", "examId": "615d76b2c52ffa3c944600df", "heldOn": "2005-04-30T09:00:00.000Z", "isVisible": true, "shortName": "2005", "title": "JEE Main 2005"}, "evalStatus": "notAttempted", "lastPracticed": null}, {"_id": "648b5a61417cc3fb48d655e7", "type": "singleCorrect", "level": 1, "questionLabels": [], "previousYearPapers": [{"_id": "615d92eade3d91842a5cf7c4", "examId": "615d76b2c52ffa3c944600df", "heldOn": "2004-04-30T09:00:00.000Z", "isVisible": true, "shortName": "2004", "title": "JEE Main 2004"}], "question": {"text": "Let $S(K)=1+3+5+\\ldots+(2 K-1)=3+K^2$. Then which of the following is true?", "image": null}, "options": [{"id": "5ZsIo", "text": "\n$S(1)$ is correct\n", "image": null, "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "FtUTD", "text": "\nPrinciple of mathematical induction can be used to prove the formula\n", "image": null, "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "Kz4Ov", "text": "\n$S(K) \\neq S(K+1)$\n", "image": null, "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "ufbFo", "text": "\n$\\mathrm{S}(\\mathrm{K}) \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{S}(\\mathrm{K}+1)$", "image": null, "isCorrect": true}], "correctValue": null, "solution": {"text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& S(k)=1+3+5+\\ldots \\ldots . .+(2 k-1)=3+k^2 \\\\\n& S(k+1)=1+3+5+\\ldots \\ldots \\ldots+(2 k-1)+(2 k+1) \\\\\n& =\\left(3+k^2\\right)+2 k+1=k^2+2 k+4\\left[\\text { from } S(k)=3+k^2\\right] \\\\\n& =3+\\left(k^2+2 k+1\\right)=3+(k+1)^2=S(k+1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nAlthough $S(k)$ in itself is not true but it considered true will always imply towards $S(k+1)$.", "image": null}, "videoSolution": null, "syllabusCategory": "outOfSyllabus", "questionStructure": ["default"], "previousYear": {"_id": "615d92eade3d91842a5cf7c4", "examId": "615d76b2c52ffa3c944600df", "heldOn": "2004-04-30T09:00:00.000Z", "isVisible": true, "shortName": "2004", "title": "JEE Main 2004"}, "evalStatus": "notAttempted", "lastPracticed": null}, {"_id": "648b5a61417cc3fb48d65443", "type": "singleCorrect", "level": 3, "questionLabels": [], "previousYearPapers": [{"_id": "615d92e9de3d91842a5cf7c2", "examId": "615d76b2c52ffa3c944600df", "heldOn": "2002-04-30T09:00:00.000Z", "isVisible": true, "shortName": "2002", "title": "JEE Main 2002"}], "question": {"text": "If $a_n=\\sqrt{7+\\sqrt{7+\\sqrt{7+\\ldots .}}}$ having $\\mathrm{n}$ radical signs then by methods of mathematical induciton which is true", "image": null}, "options": [{"id": "Gn480", "text": "\n$a_n>7 \\forall n \\geq 1$\n", "image": null, "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "Ej3E2", "text": "\n$\\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{n}}>7 \\forall \\mathrm{n} \\geq 1$\n", "image": null, "isCorrect": true}, {"id": "sJILJ", "text": "\n$a_n < 4 \\forall n \\geq 1$", "image": null, "isCorrect": false}, {"id": "8cIzY", "text": "\n$a_n < 3 \\forall \\mathrm{n} \\geq 1$", "image": null, "isCorrect": false}], "correctValue": null, "solution": {"text": "$\\mathrm{a}_1=\\sqrt{7} < 7$. Leta $_{\\mathrm{m}} < 7$. Then $\\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{m}}+1=\\sqrt{7+\\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{m}}} \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{m}+1}^2=7+\\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{m}} < 7+7 < 14$\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{m}+1} < \\sqrt{14} < 7 ;$ So $\\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{n}} < 7 \\forall \\mathrm{n} \\therefore \\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{n}}>3$", "image": null}, "videoSolution": null, "syllabusCategory": "outOfSyllabus", "questionStructure": ["default"], "previousYear": {"_id": "615d92e9de3d91842a5cf7c2", "examId": "615d76b2c52ffa3c944600df", "heldOn": "2002-04-30T09:00:00.000Z", "isVisible": true, "shortName": "2002", "title": "JEE Main 2002"}, "evalStatus": "notAttempted", "lastPracticed": null}]}]}